      "summary_json": "docs/model-onboarding/hcls/openmm-md-8-5-1-wrapper-20260604Tprofiler-optimization-summary.json",
      "technical_interpretation": "Nsight Systems showed NoCutoff computeNonbonded remained the dominant GPU kernel family and cutoff neighbor-list modes were slower for this 4096-particle argon lattice. The accepted speedup is an explicit Verlet/NVE mode that removes Langevin thermostat/random-number work; use it only when NVE dynamics are scientifically acceptable. For NVT/Langevin simulations, keep LangevinMiddle and expect the previous NoCutoff single/mixed throughput numbers."
